RenPyLinter: backport SDL #16355 scene orientation support to SDL 3.4.8.
Upstream: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/commit/114aca1727c755104ecfbd3bf4db986e0ff483e2
(not in any release-3.4.x tag up to 3.4.18).
Local adaptation, as in renpylinter/sdl2's ios-scene-geometry.diff and
ios-window-size-events.diff: the orientation comes from the caller's window
scene (effectiveGeometry on iOS 26+, interfaceOrientation on iOS 13-25);
existing UIWindow bounds are used without an orientation flip; Unknown is
never treated as portrait; each window refreshes its display modes from its
own scene on layout. SDL3's UIKit driver already reports fullscreen
dimensions itself, so SDL_video.c needs no change. The camera backend is
not built (SDL_CAMERA=OFF) and is left unchanged. Applied after Ren'Py's
sdl3-opengl-ios.diff and sdl3-metalangle.diff.

